                        <field name="dc_subject">Ferdinand VII, King of Spain, 1784-1833 </field>
                        <field name="dc_title">Mr. Secretary of State and the Office of the Interior of the Peninsula... I communicate the circular issued by the Ministry of Grace and Justice... [Printed text]: That the captains general, commanders, governors and justice of the peoples of the border do not allow to enter Spain with any pretext: 1st He who has served the government intruding as adviser or minister. 2nd He who, being formerly employed by S.M. of embaxador [sic] or minister, secretary of embaxada [sic] or ministry, or consul, has later admitted power, appointment or confirmation of that government, or continued in qualquiera [sic] of these orders in his name... </field>
